# Component styling

Every component folder has a `styles.ts`. The component file owns structure and behavior;
`styles.ts` owns every Tailwind class, `cva()` variant, and shadcn `className`.

## What lives in `styles.ts`

- Every Tailwind class string, including one-liners (`flex`, `gap-2`, a single color).
- `cva()` variant tables and their exported `VariantProps` type.
- `cn()`-composed class strings and class-building helpers (`row(isSelected)`).

```ts
// features/orders/ui/order-card/styles.ts
import { cn } from '@/shared/lib/utils';

export const root = (className?: string) => cn('flex items-center gap-3', className);
export const title = 'text-sm font-medium text-foreground';
export const amount = 'ms-auto text-sm font-semibold text-foreground';
```

```tsx
// features/orders/ui/order-card/order-card.tsx
import { Card } from '@/shared/ui/card';
import * as styles from './styles';
import type { OrderCardProps } from './types';

export const OrderCard = ({ order, className }: OrderCardProps): JSX.Element => (
  <Card className={styles.root(className)}>
    <p className={styles.title}>
      {order.reference}
    </p>
    <span className={styles.amount}>
      {order.formattedTotal}
    </span>
  </Card>
);
```

## JSX never carries classes

- No string, template, or `cn('…')` literal in a `className` prop. `className={styles.x}` or
  `className={styles.x(className)}` only.
- No `style={{}}`, CSS Modules, styled-components, or `!important`.
- A conditional class is a function in `styles.ts` (`styles.row(isSelected)`) or a `cva` variant —
  never a ternary in the `className` prop.

## Primitives keep their look

- A `className` passed to a `@/shared/ui/<name>` primitive is layout only: margin, width/height,
  grid or flex placement, gap. Never color, radius, border, shadow, typography, padding, or motion.
- A new look is a new `cva` variant in `shared/ui/<name>/styles.ts` (shared-UI step), not an
  override at the call site.
- Match the prototype through theme tokens in `shared/ui/theme/globals.css` (`--primary`,
  `--radius`, fonts) — not by restyling primitives per feature.

## Motion

- Open/close motion belongs to the shadcn base: the registry's `animate-in`, `animate-out`,
  `fade-*`, `zoom-*`, `slide-*`, `duration-*`, and `data-[state=*]` classes, verbatim, in
  `shared/ui/<name>/styles.ts`.
- Outside `shared/ui/`, no `animate-*`, `transition-*`, `duration-*`, `delay-*`, `ease-*`, `fade-*`,
  `slide-*`, `zoom-*` utility, and no new `@keyframes` or `--animate-*` in global CSS. These fight
  the primitive's own `data-state` animation.
- Prototype motion (`reveal`, `hover-lift`, staggered entrances) is not ported. A spinner is
  `@/shared/ui/spinner`; a placeholder is `@/shared/ui/skeleton`.

## Contract

- `styles.ts` exports plain values and, when variants exist, the derived `VariantProps` type.
- The component passes an incoming `className` into that export so a caller can still override layout.
- Colors are semantic tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`). No raw hex or palette-step classes.
- One light palette. No `dark:` variants.

Load `tailwind-styles` for `cva()` authoring and `shadcn-usage` for primitive composition.
